+// Occupancy returns the number of descriptors the kernel has delivered but we
+// have not yet released (producer - consumer). It is NON-destructive (it does
+// not advance the cached consumer, so it does not steal descriptors from the
+// dispatch loop's Peek) and thread-safe (both producer and consumer are shared
+// atomic values). A persistently-high occupancy (the ring full and not
+// draining) is the data-plane wedge signal (the eBPF guard is still
+// redirecting frames to the socket, but the socket's ring is not draining).
+// An empty ring (0) means idle (no traffic).
+func (rq *RXQueue) Occupancy() uint32 {
+	return rq.producer.Load() - rq.consumer.RacyLoad()
+}
